<Programs>
<Program Name="MainProgram" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Main" Disabled="false" UseAsFolder="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Main" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scan order]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First scan: clear every HMI request bit so nothing acts on power-up.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)[OTU(HMI_AckAll),OTU(HMI_LTReset),OTU(P1.HMI_Reset),OTU(P2.HMI_Reset)];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scan order: inputs, level, lead/lag, pumps, alarms, outputs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R01_Inputs,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R02_Level,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R03_LeadLag,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R10_Pump1,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R11_Pump2,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R20_Alarms,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R30_Outputs,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R01_Inputs" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[I/O mapping: field inputs to pump structures]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Map field inputs once, here. Replace the DI_ placeholder tags with module tags (Local:x:I.Data.n) at commissioning.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P1_Auto)OTE(P1.HOA_Auto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P1_Hand)OTE(P1.HOA_Hand);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P1_RunFbk)OTE(P1.RunFbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Overload contact is normally closed: an open contact (or a broken wire) is a trip.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(DI_P1_OL_OK)OTE(P1.OL_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P2_Auto)OTE(P2.HOA_Auto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P2_Hand)OTE(P2.HOA_Hand);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(DI_P2_RunFbk)OTE(P2.RunFbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Overload contact is normally closed: an open contact (or a broken wire) is a trip.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(DI_P2_OL_OK)OTE(P2.OL_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R02_Level" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Level scaling, transmitter checks, setpoint validation]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scale LT-101 4-20 mA to 0-100 % of wet well span.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SCP(AI_LT101_mA,4.0,20.0,0.0,100.0,LT101_Pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Signal fault per NAMUR NE 43: below 3.6 mA (broken wire) or above 21 mA, filtered 2 s.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(AI_LT101_mA,3.6),GRT(AI_LT101_mA,21.0)]TON(LT101_FltTmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(LT101_FltTmr.DN)OTE(LT101_Fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Disagreement limits: transmitter must read below AllOff + 10 % when the low float is low, and above HighAlm - 10 % when the high-high float is high.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[ADD(SPV_AllOff,10.0,LT_DisLoLim)SUB(SPV_HighAlm,10.0,LT_DisHiLim);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[A stuck transmitter is caught by the floats within 5 s and latched; operator resets from the HMI once the readings agree.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(DI_LSL)GRT(LT101_Pct,LT_DisLoLim),XIO(DI_LSHH)LES(LT101_Pct,LT_DisHiLim)]TON(LT_Dis_Tmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(LT_Dis_Tmr.DN)OTL(LT_Disagree);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_LTReset)XIO(LT_Dis_Tmr.DN)OTU(LT_Disagree);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_LTReset)OTU(HMI_LTReset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Transmitter unusable: control falls back to the floats.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(LT101_Fault),XIC(LT_Disagree)]OTE(LT101_Bad);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[HMI setpoint checks: each band at least 5 % apart, alarm above lag start, all within 5-95 %.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[ADD(SP_AllOff,5.0,SP_Chk1)ADD(SP_LeadOn,5.0,SP_Chk2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(SP_LeadOn,SP_Chk1)GEQ(SP_LagOn,SP_Chk2)GRT(SP_HighAlm,SP_LagOn)LIM(5.0,SP_AllOff,95.0)LIM(5.0,SP_HighAlm,95.0)OTE(SP_Valid);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Only validated setpoints reach the control logic; a bad entry keeps the last good set and raises ALM_SPInvalid.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SP_Valid)MOV(SP_LeadOn,SPV_LeadOn)MOV(SP_LagOn,SPV_LagOn)MOV(SP_AllOff,SPV_AllOff)MOV(SP_HighAlm,SPV_HighAlm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R03_LeadLag" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Level control, float backup, alternation, lead assignment]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Lead demand from the transmitter: on at LeadOn, sealed in until AllOff.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(LT101_Bad)[GEQ(LT101_Pct,SPV_LeadOn),XIC(Lead_Dmd)GRT(LT101_Pct,SPV_AllOff)]OTE(Lead_Dmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Lag demand from the transmitter: on at LagOn, sealed in until AllOff.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(LT101_Bad)[GEQ(LT101_Pct,SPV_LagOn),XIC(Lag_Dmd)GRT(LT101_Pct,SPV_AllOff)]OTE(Lag_Dmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Float backup (transmitter bad): both pumps from the high-high float down to the low float.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(LT101_Bad)XIO(DI_LSHH)OTL(Bkp_Dmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(LT101_Bad),XIO(DI_LSL)]OTU(Bkp_Dmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Low float is a hard cut-out for both modes (dry-run protection).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Lead_Dmd),XIC(Bkp_Dmd)]XIC(DI_LSL)OTE(Lead_Call);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Lag starts 3 s after the lead call to stagger inrush.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Lag_Dmd),XIC(Bkp_Dmd)]XIC(DI_LSL)XIC(Lead_Call)TON(Lag_Stagger,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Lag_Stagger.DN)OTE(Lag_Call);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Alternate at the end of every lead cycle (falling edge of Lead_Call).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Lead_Call)OSF(Alt_OSF_Sto,Alt_Pulse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Alt_Pulse)ADD(Lead_Idx,1,Lead_Idx);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(Lead_Idx,2)MOV(0,Lead_Idx);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Effective lead: the alternator's choice if available, otherwise the other pump (automatic fail-over).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Lead_Idx,0)XIC(P1.Avail),EQU(Lead_Idx,1)XIO(P2.Avail)]OTE(P1_IsLead);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(P1_IsLead)OTE(P2_IsLead);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump calls: lead call to the effective lead, lag call to the other pump.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Lead_Call)XIC(P1_IsLead),XIC(Lag_Call)XIC(P2_IsLead)]OTE(P1.Call);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Lead_Call)XIC(P2_IsLead),XIC(Lag_Call)XIC(P1_IsLead)]OTE(P2.Call);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R10_Pump1" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Pump P-101]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 fault: failed to start. Run command present but no contactor feedback within FTS_Tmr (5 s).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Cmd_Run)XIO(P1.RunFbk)TON(P1.FTS_Tmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.FTS_Tmr.DN)OTL(P1.Flt_FTS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 fault: overload relay tripped.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.OL_Trip)OTL(P1.Flt_OL);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 fault reset from HMI. Refused while the overload is still tripped. The request bit is always cleared by the PLC (handshake), so a lost HMI connection cannot leave it set.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.HMI_Reset)XIO(P1.OL_Trip)[OTU(P1.Flt_FTS),OTU(P1.Flt_OL)];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.HMI_Reset)OTU(P1.HMI_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 fault summary (after the reset rungs, so a reset takes effect in the same scan). Uncommanded run is alarm-only and does not remove the pump from service.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(P1.Flt_FTS),XIC(P1.Flt_OL)]OTE(P1.Fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 available for automatic control: AUTO, no latched fault, not taken out of service on the HMI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.HOA_Auto)XIO(P1.Fault)XIO(P1.HMI_OOS)OTE(P1.Avail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 run command (AUTO only; HAND is hardwired at the starter).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Call)XIC(P1.Avail)OTE(P1.Cmd_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 running without a command in AUTO (welded contactor, wiring fault) for 3 s.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.RunFbk)XIO(P1.Cmd_Run)XIO(P1.HOA_Hand)TON(P1.Uncmd_Tmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Uncmd_Tmr.DN)OTE(P1.Flt_Uncmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P1 start counter: one count per start, on the feedback rising edge.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.RunFbk)ONS(P1.Start_ONS)ADD(P1.Starts,1,P1.Starts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R11_Pump2" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Pump P-102]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 fault: failed to start. Run command present but no contactor feedback within FTS_Tmr (5 s).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Cmd_Run)XIO(P2.RunFbk)TON(P2.FTS_Tmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.FTS_Tmr.DN)OTL(P2.Flt_FTS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 fault: overload relay tripped.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.OL_Trip)OTL(P2.Flt_OL);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 fault reset from HMI. Refused while the overload is still tripped. The request bit is always cleared by the PLC (handshake), so a lost HMI connection cannot leave it set.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.HMI_Reset)XIO(P2.OL_Trip)[OTU(P2.Flt_FTS),OTU(P2.Flt_OL)];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.HMI_Reset)OTU(P2.HMI_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 fault summary (after the reset rungs, so a reset takes effect in the same scan). Uncommanded run is alarm-only and does not remove the pump from service.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(P2.Flt_FTS),XIC(P2.Flt_OL)]OTE(P2.Fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 available for automatic control: AUTO, no latched fault, not taken out of service on the HMI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.HOA_Auto)XIO(P2.Fault)XIO(P2.HMI_OOS)OTE(P2.Avail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 run command (AUTO only; HAND is hardwired at the starter).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Call)XIC(P2.Avail)OTE(P2.Cmd_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 running without a command in AUTO (welded contactor, wiring fault) for 3 s.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.RunFbk)XIO(P2.Cmd_Run)XIO(P2.HOA_Hand)TON(P2.Uncmd_Tmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Uncmd_Tmr.DN)OTE(P2.Flt_Uncmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[P2 start counter: one count per start, on the feedback rising edge.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.RunFbk)ONS(P2.Start_ONS)ADD(P2.Starts,1,P2.Starts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R20_Alarms" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Alarm conditions, template, acknowledge, beacon]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[High level from the transmitter, or high-high float (always).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(LT101_Pct,SPV_HighAlm)XIO(LT101_Bad),XIO(DI_LSHH)]OTE(ALM_HighLevel.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(DI_LSHH)OTE(ALM_HiHiFloat.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(LT101_Bad)OTE(ALM_LT101.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Fault)OTE(ALM_P1_Fault.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Fault)OTE(ALM_P2_Fault.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Flt_Uncmd)OTE(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Flt_Uncmd)OTE(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(P1.Avail)XIO(P2.Avail)OTE(ALM_NoPump.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(SP_Valid)OTE(ALM_SPInvalid.Cond);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Alarm template, repeated per alarm: on-delay, active, and a new-alarm edge that sets Unack.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HighLevel.Cond)TON(ALM_HighLevel.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HighLevel.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_HighLevel.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HighLevel.Active)ONS(ALM_HighLevel.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_HighLevel.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_HighLevel.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HiHiFloat.Cond)TON(ALM_HiHiFloat.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HiHiFloat.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_HiHiFloat.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_HiHiFloat.Active)ONS(ALM_HiHiFloat.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_HiHiFloat.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_HiHiFloat.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_LT101.Cond)TON(ALM_LT101.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_LT101.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_LT101.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_LT101.Active)ONS(ALM_LT101.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_LT101.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_LT101.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Fault.Cond)TON(ALM_P1_Fault.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Fault.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_P1_Fault.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Fault.Active)ONS(ALM_P1_Fault.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_P1_Fault.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_P1_Fault.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Fault.Cond)TON(ALM_P2_Fault.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Fault.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_P2_Fault.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Fault.Active)ONS(ALM_P2_Fault.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_P2_Fault.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_P2_Fault.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Cond)TON(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Active)ONS(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Cond)TON(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Active)ONS(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_NoPump.Cond)TON(ALM_NoPump.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_NoPump.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_NoPump.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_NoPump.Active)ONS(ALM_NoPump.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_NoPump.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_NoPump.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_SPInvalid.Cond)TON(ALM_SPInvalid.Dly,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_SPInvalid.Dly.DN)OTE(ALM_SPInvalid.Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_SPInvalid.Active)ONS(ALM_SPInvalid.Edge_ONS)OTL(ALM_SPInvalid.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(ALM_SPInvalid.Unack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Acknowledge handshake: the PLC clears the HMI request after use.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AckAll)OTU(HMI_AckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Beacon while any alarm is unacknowledged.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(ALM_HighLevel.Unack),XIC(ALM_HiHiFloat.Unack),XIC(ALM_LT101.Unack),XIC(ALM_P1_Fault.Unack),XIC(ALM_P2_Fault.Unack),XIC(ALM_P1_Uncmd.Unack),XIC(ALM_P2_Uncmd.Unack),XIC(ALM_NoPump.Unack),XIC(ALM_SPInvalid.Unack)]OTE(ALM_AnyUnack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R30_Outputs" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output mapping]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Map outputs once, here. Replace DO_ placeholders with module tags at commissioning.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.Cmd_Run)OTE(DO_P1_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.Cmd_Run)OTE(DO_P2_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALM_AnyUnack)OTE(DO_Beacon);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Name="Totals" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Totals" Disabled="false" UseAsFolder="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Totals" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Runs every 1000 ms in periodic task T1000ms]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Run seconds counted in a 1 s periodic task: exact, independent of continuous-task scan time (no self-resetting timer drift).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P1.RunFbk)ADD(P1.RunSec,1,P1.RunSec);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(P2.RunFbk)ADD(P2.RunSec,1,P2.RunSec);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(P1.RunSec,3600.0,P1.RunHrs)DIV(P2.RunSec,3600.0,P2.RunHrs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
<Tasks>
<Task Name="MainTask" Type="CONTINUOUS" Priority="10" Watchdog="500" DisableUpdateOutputs="false" InhibitTask="false">
<ScheduledPrograms>
<ScheduledProgram Name="MainProgram"/>
</ScheduledPrograms>
</Task>
<Task Name="T1000ms" Type="PERIODIC" Rate="1000" Priority="5" Watchdog="500" DisableUpdateOutputs="false" InhibitTask="false">
<ScheduledPrograms>
<ScheduledProgram Name="Totals"/>
</ScheduledPrograms>
</Task>
</Tasks>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
